1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:02,010
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:02,010 --> 00:00:03,210
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:06,010 --> 00:00:07,810
What are you doing right now?

4
00:00:08,310 --> 00:00:09,450
Hurry up and get up.

5
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:13,320
I can't live in a house like this,
so look for another place right now.

6
00:00:13,420 --> 00:00:15,520
I'm not moving
a single step from here.

7
00:00:16,860 --> 00:00:17,890
This is unbelievable, really.

8
00:00:18,460 --> 00:00:22,030
Even if my life has hit rock bottom
since I met you,

9
00:00:22,430 --> 00:00:23,430
this is just not right.

10
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:25,130
(Episode 14)

11
00:00:29,070 --> 00:00:31,840
Come on, just take
a good look around.

12
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:34,170
The landlord said
they would clean up...

13
00:00:34,470 --> 00:00:37,040
any flooding
during the rainy season.

14
00:00:37,310 --> 00:00:40,950
For a place like this,
it is actually very well maintained.

15
00:00:41,150 --> 00:00:44,120
What? So you're saying
it could actually flood here?

16
00:00:44,820 --> 00:00:48,090
No. That's not what I meant.

17
00:00:50,620 --> 00:00:53,220
Don't you know Ye Ri
is discussing marriage...

18
00:00:53,220 --> 00:00:54,690
with the son of her company's CEO?

19
00:00:55,560 --> 00:00:58,630
She might become the future wife
of Hwanggeum Apparel's CEO,

20
00:00:58,960 --> 00:01:01,630
so how could you possibly make her
live in a place like this?

21
00:01:01,930 --> 00:01:05,570
This must be a dream.
It has to be a dream.

22
00:01:07,770 --> 00:01:10,280
Tell me right now.
Hey, Kang Hak Sung.

23
00:01:10,340 --> 00:01:13,180
Hey, tell me this is a dream.
Hurry up.

24
00:01:13,480 --> 00:01:15,510
"Hey?" Did you just say "hey?"

25
00:01:15,810 --> 00:01:18,080
Yes, I did. What are you going to do
about it?

26
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:21,990
What are you going to do
about my life and Ye Ri's life?

27
00:01:27,590 --> 00:01:29,230
They are not even dating yet.

28
00:01:29,460 --> 00:01:31,060
I told you not to get ahead
of yourself, didn't I?

29
00:01:31,130 --> 00:01:32,130
I don't care.

30
00:01:32,660 --> 00:01:34,530
Cancel the lease right now.
I refuse to accept this.

31
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:38,800
Fine, if you can't live here,
then you can move out.

32
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:40,470
With what I can afford right now,

33
00:01:41,370 --> 00:01:42,710
we should be grateful
for this place.

34
00:01:48,750 --> 00:01:51,180
Honey. Hey!

35
00:02:00,660 --> 00:02:01,890
(Moving 24 Express)

36
00:02:01,990 --> 00:02:02,990
Here we go.

37
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:10,640
I'm here, Mom.

38
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:15,210
Mom... Wait, Dad.
Is this where we're living?

39
00:02:15,470 --> 00:02:18,280
Yes, it is.
I put your things in your room,

40
00:02:18,340 --> 00:02:19,780
so you can go finish unpacking.

41
00:02:22,450 --> 00:02:23,450
You're here?

42
00:02:24,050 --> 00:02:26,420
Mom, what in the world is going on?

43
00:02:26,890 --> 00:02:28,790
I thought we lived upstairs
and went to the wrong door.

44
00:02:29,350 --> 00:02:31,660
I only found out today
while moving our stuff.

45
00:02:32,790 --> 00:02:35,060
I honestly don't know what to say.

46
00:02:37,160 --> 00:02:38,260
Talk to me for a second.

47
00:02:38,930 --> 00:02:40,330
- What?
- Come on.

48
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:42,000
Honey...

49
00:02:50,310 --> 00:02:51,840
I can accept living in a multiplex.

50
00:02:52,240 --> 00:02:53,780
But you never mentioned
it was a semi-basement.

51
00:02:54,610 --> 00:02:55,980
I didn't know either, sweetie.

52
00:02:56,050 --> 00:02:58,420
If I had known, do you think
I would've agreed to move here?

53
00:02:58,750 --> 00:03:01,390
Now that I'm finally ready to make
a real move on Team Leader Cha,

54
00:03:01,550 --> 00:03:03,150
what will he think of me
when he finds out...

55
00:03:03,150 --> 00:03:04,690
I live in a place like this?

56
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:08,830
Don't worry.
Even if it means divorcing your dad,

57
00:03:09,090 --> 00:03:10,860
I'm going to get us out
of this house no matter what.

58
00:03:11,460 --> 00:03:12,460
Are you serious?

59
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:16,330
Well, we just have to stay here
for now.

60
00:03:16,530 --> 00:03:17,900
So you have no plan.

61
00:03:18,570 --> 00:03:20,410
I told you I should look
into a loan, didn't I?

62
00:03:20,710 --> 00:03:23,010
I trusted you, Mom,
and look where we are.

63
00:03:23,680 --> 00:03:25,610
Even a rented apartment
would be fine.

64
00:03:25,680 --> 00:03:28,550
We need to live somewhere
that looks decent to other people.

65
00:03:29,050 --> 00:03:30,920
I'll try to come up with something,

66
00:03:30,920 --> 00:03:32,350
so just bear with it
a little longer.

67
00:03:32,850 --> 00:03:34,120
If I had my way,

68
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:36,920
I would kick your dad to the curb
right this second.

69
00:03:38,060 --> 00:03:40,760
I had a bad feeling about this
since you said we were moving here.

70
00:03:41,160 --> 00:03:42,930
What is this place, seriously?

71
00:03:43,630 --> 00:03:45,830
- A bug!
- Where?

72
00:03:46,160 --> 00:03:48,330
Where? Honey!

73
00:03:48,630 --> 00:03:51,700
Honey, there is a bug here!

74
00:03:53,770 --> 00:03:57,440
Honey, what are you doing?
Come here and catch this bug.

75
00:04:05,320 --> 00:04:07,620
Wait, where did my tablet go?

76
00:04:08,320 --> 00:04:10,090
I definitely put it in here.

77
00:04:13,890 --> 00:04:17,230
Why do you have my things?

78
00:04:18,200 --> 00:04:19,200
Where did you get them?

79
00:04:19,260 --> 00:04:20,770
I picked them up over there
on my way.

80
00:04:20,830 --> 00:04:22,870
Why do you drop
your things everywhere?

81
00:04:23,170 --> 00:04:24,370
What are you,

82
00:04:24,970 --> 00:04:26,470
Hansel and Gretel?

83
00:04:29,210 --> 00:04:32,140
Don't tell me Jaden Cha...

84
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:35,350
took my tablet?

85
00:04:37,820 --> 00:04:40,550
Right, when I was running
in a hurry,

86
00:04:40,620 --> 00:04:42,720
things fell out of my bag
one by one.

87
00:04:43,150 --> 00:04:45,820
And Jaden Cha, or whatever his name is,
picked them up.

88
00:04:47,030 --> 00:04:49,730
And out of all of them,
only my most expensive tablet...

89
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:52,760
That's it.
He saw it and couldn't resist it.

90
00:04:52,830 --> 00:04:54,370
He must've been tempted
and taken my...

91
00:04:55,870 --> 00:04:56,900
Wait, but...

92
00:04:57,140 --> 00:04:59,900
why would a guy staying
in a top-tier hotel suite do that?

93
00:05:01,010 --> 00:05:03,270
Especially a globally successful
designer?

94
00:05:06,680 --> 00:05:08,150
He must be a kleptomaniac.

95
00:05:09,110 --> 00:05:11,420
He must relieve his stress
by stealing.

96
00:05:13,890 --> 00:05:16,250
But why did he have to steal
the precious tablet...

97
00:05:16,250 --> 00:05:19,360
that I bought
with my blood, sweat, and tears,

98
00:05:19,420 --> 00:05:21,960
and which I poured
my entire soul into?

99
00:05:24,830 --> 00:05:26,960
Oh, I'm sorry.

100
00:05:39,310 --> 00:05:40,880
Gosh, it's been
a really long time...

101
00:05:40,950 --> 00:05:42,750
since I saw a design
with this much to criticize.

102
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:01,100
Don't tell me that guy...

103
00:06:01,330 --> 00:06:04,170
is going to sell my tablet
on some secondhand marketplace...

104
00:06:04,240 --> 00:06:05,670
or something?

105
00:06:06,640 --> 00:06:09,210
No. If it is because of kleptomania,

106
00:06:09,410 --> 00:06:12,040
he probably just stole it
to keep it.

107
00:06:13,380 --> 00:06:14,980
I have to find it no matter what.

108
00:06:15,450 --> 00:06:18,420
I need that to go to Paris
or New York.

109
00:06:18,480 --> 00:06:21,090
All my portfolios are in there.

110
00:06:22,020 --> 00:06:25,520
Just wait until I catch him.
What a total jerk.

111
00:06:27,530 --> 00:06:28,530
Hey.

112
00:06:29,960 --> 00:06:31,200
Why are you standing there...

113
00:06:31,260 --> 00:06:32,960
muttering to yourself
like a crazy person?

114
00:06:34,930 --> 00:06:36,900
It's nothing.

115
00:06:38,040 --> 00:06:39,340
Did you go to the convenience store?

116
00:06:39,600 --> 00:06:43,010
Yes, I think
I might've had a light dinner.

117
00:06:43,240 --> 00:06:45,180
I was craving cup noodles
and a triangle-shaped gimbap.

118
00:06:45,180 --> 00:06:46,580
I couldn't resist.

119
00:06:47,950 --> 00:06:50,080
If you are going to eat,
just pick one.

120
00:06:50,150 --> 00:06:52,350
You will be in trouble
if you eat everything you crave.

121
00:06:52,750 --> 00:06:54,920
You already look
a bit bloated lately.

122
00:06:55,690 --> 00:06:56,790
What?

123
00:06:57,090 --> 00:07:00,290
Hey.
Are you trying to get on my nerves,

124
00:07:00,360 --> 00:07:02,890
or do I really look bloated?

125
00:07:04,830 --> 00:07:06,730
It tastes better
when you eat with someone.

126
00:07:08,370 --> 00:07:09,370
Seriously.

127
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:12,100
I'm home.

128
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:15,040
Mom.

129
00:07:16,270 --> 00:07:18,910
I'm here. Mom.

130
00:07:24,220 --> 00:07:26,550
Three times nine is 27.

131
00:07:26,620 --> 00:07:29,390
Three times eight is 24.

132
00:07:29,450 --> 00:07:32,020
Three times seven is 20...

133
00:07:34,490 --> 00:07:36,760
Twenty, so...

134
00:07:37,260 --> 00:07:38,960
It's 21, Great-Grandma.

135
00:07:39,130 --> 00:07:40,200
Goodness.

136
00:07:40,600 --> 00:07:43,330
My sweet girl has memorized
the multiplication table.

137
00:07:43,330 --> 00:07:46,970
You've been repeating the threes
all day, Great-Grandma.

138
00:07:46,970 --> 00:07:48,940
You're so smart.

139
00:07:48,940 --> 00:07:51,510
We might have a doctor
in the family.

140
00:07:53,740 --> 00:07:54,750
Yes.

141
00:07:55,710 --> 00:07:57,010
I'm home, Grandma.

142
00:07:57,820 --> 00:07:59,450
The house is so quiet.

143
00:07:59,720 --> 00:08:00,720
It is.

144
00:08:01,320 --> 00:08:02,890
It has been gloomy all day.

145
00:08:03,320 --> 00:08:04,990
We will talk about it
tomorrow morning,

146
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:06,160
so go upstairs and rest.

147
00:08:06,720 --> 00:08:09,790
Okay.
Su Ah, do you want to sleep with me?

148
00:08:09,860 --> 00:08:12,360
- So Grandma can sleep comfortably?
- No.

149
00:08:12,430 --> 00:08:15,400
Great-Grandma said
she would tell me a story.

150
00:08:15,630 --> 00:08:18,600
- Right?
- Yes, of course.

151
00:08:19,070 --> 00:08:21,540
I'll tell you the story
of the tortoise and the hare.

152
00:08:24,140 --> 00:08:26,480
- Good night, Grandma.
- Good night.

153
00:08:29,650 --> 00:08:30,680
Come here.

154
00:08:35,620 --> 00:08:36,620
Hey, Kang Da Mi.

155
00:08:37,420 --> 00:08:38,920
Just head on upstairs. Okay?

156
00:08:39,360 --> 00:08:40,360
Why, Aunt Ri Ja?

157
00:08:41,330 --> 00:08:45,230
Your mom has been lying down
with a headache all day.

158
00:08:45,830 --> 00:08:48,330
Now that Mrs. Choi knows,
maybe she finally relaxed,

159
00:08:48,700 --> 00:08:51,500
but she just popped headache pills
and hasn't eaten a thing today.

160
00:08:52,700 --> 00:08:55,340
You should've made her
go to the hospital, then.

161
00:08:57,440 --> 00:09:00,750
Right, I'm the easy target,
you brat.

162
00:09:00,950 --> 00:09:03,150
Gosh.
My noodles are going to get soggy.

163
00:09:06,980 --> 00:09:08,050
Mom.

164
00:09:09,990 --> 00:09:12,460
I heard you haven't eaten
anything all day.

165
00:09:12,790 --> 00:09:13,820
Are you very sick?

166
00:09:14,530 --> 00:09:16,160
Should we go
to the emergency room now?

167
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:21,400
Grandma seems to be fine,

168
00:09:21,870 --> 00:09:24,170
so why are you lying
in bed like this?

169
00:09:25,340 --> 00:09:27,200
Should I make you some porridge?

170
00:09:27,910 --> 00:09:28,910
Did you eat dinner?

171
00:09:30,140 --> 00:09:32,510
Of course. Look at the time.

172
00:09:37,210 --> 00:09:39,620
My daughter. Da Mi.

173
00:09:41,090 --> 00:09:44,790
Yes? Mom, do you need something?
Just tell me.

174
00:09:46,860 --> 00:09:49,860
How much money have you saved up?

175
00:09:51,630 --> 00:09:52,630
Money?

176
00:09:53,460 --> 00:09:55,430
Yes, how much do you have?

177
00:09:56,770 --> 00:09:59,200
Why are you asking me that
all of a sudden?

178
00:10:00,970 --> 00:10:02,910
I'm just asking.

179
00:10:04,210 --> 00:10:05,640
Forget it
if you don't want to tell me.

180
00:10:06,710 --> 00:10:08,650
No, it's not that I don't want to.

181
00:10:08,780 --> 00:10:10,250
It's just
I'm just a little taken aback.

182
00:10:12,280 --> 00:10:13,880
A little over 200,000 dollars.

183
00:10:14,820 --> 00:10:16,750
Why are you asking me that
all of a sudden?

184
00:10:18,660 --> 00:10:21,590
Come on.
I'm different from my brothers, Mom.

185
00:10:22,230 --> 00:10:23,390
Even though I keep failing...

186
00:10:23,430 --> 00:10:24,900
the fashion company
internship contests,

187
00:10:25,200 --> 00:10:27,260
I want to go to a fashion school
in Paris or New York.

188
00:10:27,700 --> 00:10:29,800
I've been working
at the department store,

189
00:10:29,870 --> 00:10:31,540
cutting expenses
and saving every penny.

190
00:10:32,100 --> 00:10:34,070
You don't have to worry
about me, Mom.

191
00:10:35,510 --> 00:10:37,740
It's not because
I'm worried about you.

192
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:40,680
Actually...

193
00:10:43,210 --> 00:10:45,350
Mom, don't tell me...

194
00:10:46,150 --> 00:10:48,520
you want me to help Dae Chi...

195
00:10:50,320 --> 00:10:51,860
No, it's nothing like that.

196
00:10:52,720 --> 00:10:53,720
You must be tired.

197
00:10:54,230 --> 00:10:55,390
Hurry upstairs and get some rest.

198
00:11:16,110 --> 00:11:17,450
Oh, come on.

199
00:11:18,020 --> 00:11:20,480
Go wash your feet first, Gang Nam.
They smell rotten.

200
00:11:20,550 --> 00:11:22,620
Hey, let's just go to sleep.

201
00:11:22,950 --> 00:11:26,460
Both you and I have had
our heads down all day.

202
00:11:26,860 --> 00:11:27,930
Aren't you tired?

203
00:11:28,190 --> 00:11:29,890
What did we even do to be tired?

204
00:11:31,830 --> 00:11:34,270
Go wash up.
And brush your teeth, too.

205
00:11:36,330 --> 00:11:37,440
I don't smell anything.

206
00:11:37,800 --> 00:11:40,670
Seriously, you nag
even worse than a wife.

207
00:11:41,070 --> 00:11:43,140
All right, I'll go wash up, okay?

208
00:11:43,770 --> 00:11:44,780
Goodness.

209
00:11:45,940 --> 00:11:46,940
Gang Nam, sit down.

210
00:11:47,180 --> 00:11:48,750
Hey, who do you think
you're ordering around?

211
00:11:49,110 --> 00:11:50,110
I said sit down.

212
00:11:51,350 --> 00:11:52,920
Seriously.

213
00:11:54,850 --> 00:11:56,490
I'm sitting. What now?

214
00:11:58,990 --> 00:12:00,760
What are you two planning to do now?

215
00:12:03,330 --> 00:12:04,960
What did you two do all day today?

216
00:12:05,700 --> 00:12:07,330
Did you just put your heads together
and play patty-cake?

217
00:12:08,900 --> 00:12:10,030
Mom couldn't even go
to the restaurant...

218
00:12:10,100 --> 00:12:11,670
and had to stay in bed all day.

219
00:12:12,270 --> 00:12:13,470
You aren't cockroaches.

220
00:12:13,540 --> 00:12:15,370
Are you going to hide in your room
after causing trouble...

221
00:12:15,540 --> 00:12:18,940
and wait for Grandma or Mom
to fix everything for you?

222
00:12:20,380 --> 00:12:21,380
Hey.

223
00:12:22,750 --> 00:12:24,180
Did you just call us cockroaches?

224
00:12:24,720 --> 00:12:26,450
Yes, she did.

225
00:12:26,950 --> 00:12:28,720
She definitely said cockroaches.

226
00:12:28,920 --> 00:12:31,090
Listen up, Kkangda.
Even if your brothers...

227
00:12:31,460 --> 00:12:34,020
unfortunately managed
to cause massive trouble...

228
00:12:34,830 --> 00:12:36,860
at the exact same time,

229
00:12:38,300 --> 00:12:41,070
does that give you, the youngest,
the right to glare at us...

230
00:12:41,070 --> 00:12:42,170
like you want to eat us alive?

231
00:12:42,700 --> 00:12:45,600
We're your older brothers, you punk.

232
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:47,940
Yes, who said you weren't?

233
00:12:47,940 --> 00:12:49,270
It's only because
you're my brothers...

234
00:12:49,270 --> 00:12:51,440
that I'm even talking
to you right now.

235
00:12:52,840 --> 00:12:55,850
Mom raised the three of us
without a father,

236
00:12:55,910 --> 00:12:58,450
and she hasn't had a single day
of proper rest until now.

237
00:12:59,020 --> 00:13:01,890
She's been taking care of Grandma
and even looking after our aunt.

238
00:13:02,290 --> 00:13:04,590
She has done nothing
but sacrifice herself her entire life.

239
00:13:04,820 --> 00:13:06,320
We should be doing everything
we can to repay her,

240
00:13:06,320 --> 00:13:08,760
but what are you two
doing right now?

241
00:13:09,130 --> 00:13:10,230
And have you?

242
00:13:12,160 --> 00:13:13,300
What?

243
00:13:13,300 --> 00:13:14,930
How much have you...

244
00:13:14,930 --> 00:13:17,800
actually done for Mom
to be so confident?

245
00:13:19,340 --> 00:13:20,400
Hey, Dae Chi.

246
00:13:21,170 --> 00:13:22,910
She might not have done a lot,

247
00:13:23,540 --> 00:13:26,710
- but she is still better than us.
- She is better than us.

248
00:13:27,480 --> 00:13:30,150
But listen to what she is saying.

249
00:13:30,980 --> 00:13:33,420
She talks like she has been
the perfect daughter.

250
00:13:33,780 --> 00:13:35,590
She has never even given
a single cent...

251
00:13:35,590 --> 00:13:36,690
of her salary to the family.

252
00:13:37,860 --> 00:13:40,790
People would think
she's been providing for all of us.

253
00:13:41,560 --> 00:13:42,590
And Kkangda.

254
00:13:43,360 --> 00:13:45,360
I didn't want to say this,

255
00:13:46,060 --> 00:13:47,430
but you started it.

256
00:13:48,500 --> 00:13:50,230
What is it? Say it.

257
00:13:50,970 --> 00:13:53,800
If you have something to say,
I won't stop you.

258
00:13:54,140 --> 00:13:55,740
If anyone should be repaying her,

259
00:13:56,670 --> 00:13:58,010
shouldn't it be you?

260
00:13:59,010 --> 00:14:01,680
Hey, what are you talking about?

261
00:14:02,610 --> 00:14:04,450
Yes, Mom raised the three of us...

262
00:14:05,150 --> 00:14:08,220
all by herself after Dad left.

263
00:14:08,790 --> 00:14:10,920
So if anyone needs to repay
that debt of gratitude,

264
00:14:11,220 --> 00:14:13,290
it should be you.

265
00:14:13,720 --> 00:14:14,730
Am I wrong?

266
00:14:17,290 --> 00:14:19,260
How could you say that to me...

267
00:14:21,430 --> 00:14:22,670
Are you finished?

268
00:14:23,800 --> 00:14:25,040
Do you really mean that?

269
00:14:25,300 --> 00:14:27,240
Yes, I mean it.

270
00:14:27,240 --> 00:14:29,210
- You little punk.
- Gang Nam!

271
00:14:29,870 --> 00:14:30,870
Don't do this.

272
00:14:31,380 --> 00:14:32,380
Hey.

273
00:14:33,880 --> 00:14:34,910
This jerk...

274
00:14:35,410 --> 00:14:37,950
has lost his mind
over that 1,130,000 dollars.

275
00:14:38,920 --> 00:14:40,920
He is out of his mind.

276
00:14:41,420 --> 00:14:42,420
Da Mi.

277
00:14:43,090 --> 00:14:45,460
Don't let it get to you.

278
00:14:45,590 --> 00:14:47,730
Don't ever be hurt by this, okay?

279
00:15:00,240 --> 00:15:05,040
Hey, you can always pay back
the 1,130,000 dollars.

280
00:15:06,210 --> 00:15:09,110
With your skills,
you can pay it off.

281
00:15:10,110 --> 00:15:12,550
But the pain you caused
our youngest sister today...

282
00:15:13,420 --> 00:15:15,820
is something you will never be able
to make up for, you jerk.

283
00:15:19,090 --> 00:15:20,260
Darn it.

284
00:15:21,460 --> 00:15:23,760
What a waste of a good face.

285
00:16:32,500 --> 00:16:35,130
By the way, did you talk to Dr. Ju?

286
00:16:35,300 --> 00:16:37,970
Yes, I called him.
I'm meeting him tomorrow.

287
00:16:39,500 --> 00:16:41,640
I really don't like him.

288
00:16:42,510 --> 00:16:43,840
It's strange
he's taking a long sabbatical...

289
00:16:43,840 --> 00:16:46,010
but just treating Mother.

290
00:16:46,740 --> 00:16:49,010
Don't you think Dr. Ju is strange?

291
00:16:49,580 --> 00:16:51,680
I'm not too fond of him either.

292
00:16:52,520 --> 00:16:55,250
But I'm at least pretending
to respect him for now.

293
00:16:55,790 --> 00:16:58,520
He is the doctor Mother chose
and relies on.

294
00:16:59,690 --> 00:17:00,990
I know that,

295
00:17:03,030 --> 00:17:05,960
when we meet him this time,

296
00:17:06,030 --> 00:17:08,400
you need to make it
very clear that we are...

297
00:17:08,470 --> 00:17:10,300
deeply concerned about Mother.

298
00:17:10,900 --> 00:17:12,340
He is a very smart man.

299
00:17:12,600 --> 00:17:14,570
Even if we just point that out,

300
00:17:14,940 --> 00:17:17,880
he'll notice we're keeping a close eye
on him.

301
00:17:19,310 --> 00:17:20,440
Okay.

302
00:17:24,380 --> 00:17:26,380
You look far too serious.

303
00:17:27,850 --> 00:17:28,950
When and how...

304
00:17:29,590 --> 00:17:33,220
did my mother cross paths
with Dr. Ju?

305
00:17:34,430 --> 00:17:35,660
Ask him that too.

306
00:17:36,390 --> 00:17:37,830
I'm really curious
about that as well.

307
00:17:43,600 --> 00:17:46,500
Madam,
I went to the morning market today,

308
00:17:46,570 --> 00:17:48,540
and the gizzard shad looked fresh,
so I grilled some.

309
00:17:48,610 --> 00:17:52,040
- Please take your time and enjoy.
- It is quite plump.

310
00:17:52,540 --> 00:17:54,710
It smells delicious.

311
00:17:55,180 --> 00:17:57,180
When did you have time
to go to the morning market?

312
00:17:57,610 --> 00:17:59,950
You're so diligent, ma'am.

313
00:18:00,120 --> 00:18:02,220
I just went for a walk, that is all.

314
00:18:03,020 --> 00:18:04,960
Thank you for your hard work.
You may leave now.

315
00:18:05,120 --> 00:18:06,220
Yes, ma'am.

316
00:18:07,660 --> 00:18:09,030
- Let's eat.
- Yes.

317
00:18:09,460 --> 00:18:12,030
- Go on. Here, try some.
- Okay.

318
00:18:12,100 --> 00:18:14,800
Seung Yun,
you have the tablet, right?

319
00:18:15,070 --> 00:18:16,300
You need to return it.

320
00:18:16,970 --> 00:18:18,240
I'll take care of it.

321
00:18:19,700 --> 00:18:22,770
- What are you talking about?
- Mind your own business, Do Yun.

322
00:18:23,170 --> 00:18:24,170
Cha Se Na.

323
00:18:25,110 --> 00:18:26,540
Watch how you speak to your brother.

324
00:18:28,050 --> 00:18:29,180
I apologize, Mother.

325
00:18:30,880 --> 00:18:32,050
Do Yun,

326
00:18:32,420 --> 00:18:34,820
why have you not brought
the return receipt?

327
00:18:36,820 --> 00:18:39,020
I'm sorry, Grandma.
I'll return it today...

328
00:18:39,090 --> 00:18:40,520
and make sure
to give you the receipt.

329
00:18:40,590 --> 00:18:42,730
Don't think
you can just gloss over it.

330
00:18:43,890 --> 00:18:44,900
I won't.

331
00:18:48,670 --> 00:18:49,870
Jin Hee,

332
00:18:50,430 --> 00:18:53,270
make sure you prepare well
for the memorial service.

333
00:18:54,170 --> 00:18:55,170
Pardon?

334
00:18:55,910 --> 00:18:57,270
Did you forget?

335
00:18:58,040 --> 00:18:59,580
Of course not, Mother.

336
00:18:59,810 --> 00:19:01,310
It's the most important event
in our family.

337
00:19:02,380 --> 00:19:04,680
Don't worry. I'll prepare for it
without any issues.

338
00:19:06,880 --> 00:19:07,920
Sincerity.

339
00:19:09,090 --> 00:19:11,820
Pardon? Sorry, I missed that.

340
00:19:12,620 --> 00:19:13,620
Sincerity.

341
00:19:13,890 --> 00:19:16,560
I mean it must be done
with sincerity.

342
00:19:18,630 --> 00:19:20,330
Of course, Mother.

343
00:19:23,530 --> 00:19:26,440
Seung Yun, when will you start
going to work?

344
00:19:27,100 --> 00:19:29,740
- I plan to start tomorrow.
- Good.

345
00:19:30,040 --> 00:19:31,040
Really?

346
00:19:31,980 --> 00:19:34,650
Why?
Is there any reason I shouldn't?

347
00:19:34,980 --> 00:19:37,450
No, everything's prepared,

348
00:19:38,280 --> 00:19:42,090
but I thought you could rest
a bit more before starting.

349
00:19:42,090 --> 00:19:43,390
I'll start tomorrow.

350
00:19:44,490 --> 00:19:48,630
Gosh, he seems very determined.
Don't you think so, honey?

351
00:19:50,060 --> 00:19:51,360
Yes, he really does.

352
00:19:52,230 --> 00:19:54,900
Anyway, I'm your boss at work.

353
00:19:55,400 --> 00:19:56,930
I won't go easy on you
just because we're family.

354
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:58,000
Understood?

355
00:19:59,100 --> 00:20:00,300
Yes, I understand.

356
00:20:00,370 --> 00:20:01,870
I'll follow your lead,
Team Leader Cha.

357
00:20:09,380 --> 00:20:10,510
Have one of these too.

358
00:20:11,150 --> 00:20:12,750
(Dr. Ju)

359
00:20:19,160 --> 00:20:21,960
Did you have breakfast?

360
00:20:22,230 --> 00:20:23,260
Yes, Madam Chairwoman.

361
00:20:23,690 --> 00:20:25,260
I figured you would've
finished your meal by now,

362
00:20:25,330 --> 00:20:26,630
so I called you first.

363
00:20:26,760 --> 00:20:28,530
You're psychic.

364
00:20:28,700 --> 00:20:31,030
I just finished eating
and came back inside.

365
00:20:31,440 --> 00:20:32,470
What is the matter?

366
00:20:33,740 --> 00:20:35,840
CEO Cha In Sung wants to see me.

367
00:20:36,210 --> 00:20:37,770
I'm supposed to visit him
at the company,

368
00:20:38,410 --> 00:20:40,780
so if you have anything to tell me,
please let me know in advance.

369
00:20:41,450 --> 00:20:45,120
We have known each other
for a long time.

370
00:20:46,380 --> 00:20:49,120
Just do whatever you think is best.

371
00:20:49,250 --> 00:20:50,490
Yes, I understand.

372
00:20:52,090 --> 00:20:54,090
The weather has gotten much cooler.

373
00:20:54,490 --> 00:20:56,760
Please avoid drinking cold water.

374
00:20:57,090 --> 00:20:58,300
Please take care, Madam Chairwoman.

375
00:20:59,400 --> 00:21:00,530
Thank you.

376
00:21:01,100 --> 00:21:02,700
I'll keep that in mind.

377
00:21:09,810 --> 00:21:12,380
I was so happy when you said
you made beef radish soup.

378
00:21:13,240 --> 00:21:15,510
Did you really make this yourself?

379
00:21:16,610 --> 00:21:18,480
Grandma took out all the bones.

380
00:21:19,250 --> 00:21:20,680
Make sure you chew it well, Su Ah.

381
00:21:21,250 --> 00:21:23,990
Yes, Grandma.
You should eat too, Grandma.

382
00:21:25,660 --> 00:21:27,860
Groceries are really expensive
these days.

383
00:21:28,660 --> 00:21:29,830
It still tastes great.

384
00:21:31,800 --> 00:21:35,300
Mom. I know groceries are expensive,

385
00:21:35,770 --> 00:21:38,370
but did the cow just dip its foot
in the broth and run away?

386
00:22:09,230 --> 00:22:11,970
I told you I wasn't going to eat,
but you still brought me food, Mom.

387
00:22:29,250 --> 00:22:30,390
Goodness.

388
00:22:41,470 --> 00:22:43,400
I absolutely can't live here.

389
00:22:44,330 --> 00:22:46,370
Sweetie, if you move out,

390
00:22:46,370 --> 00:22:48,210
how am I supposed to live
in this house with your dad...

391
00:22:48,210 --> 00:22:50,310
facing each other every day?

392
00:22:50,410 --> 00:22:53,780
Having you here is the only thing
that helps me endure and keep going.

393
00:22:55,650 --> 00:22:57,580
We won't be stuck
in this house forever, Ye Ri.

394
00:22:57,750 --> 00:22:59,650
I'll do whatever it takes...

395
00:22:59,650 --> 00:23:02,750
to find a way to move us
into an apartment soon. Okay?

396
00:23:02,750 --> 00:23:04,090
Just hold on a little longer.

397
00:23:04,820 --> 00:23:09,260
With my salary, I can rent an officetel
and live on my own, Mom.

398
00:23:09,390 --> 00:23:11,660
You can just come visit me often.

399
00:23:12,200 --> 00:23:13,730
Aside from the room being too small,

400
00:23:13,900 --> 00:23:15,200
there are bugs crawling out
of everywhere.

401
00:23:15,200 --> 00:23:16,570
It's driving me crazy.

402
00:23:17,370 --> 00:23:20,070
What if someone from work
finds out I live here?

403
00:23:20,140 --> 00:23:21,840
I would be completely humiliated.

404
00:23:22,410 --> 00:23:24,410
Don't you think paying rent
for an officetel is a waste?

405
00:23:24,540 --> 00:23:26,240
That's just throwing
your hard-earned money away.

406
00:23:26,310 --> 00:23:28,040
You need to save up every penny...

407
00:23:28,040 --> 00:23:29,180
so you can afford
your wedding expenses later.

408
00:23:30,910 --> 00:23:32,220
I have a plan.

409
00:23:32,650 --> 00:23:35,050
I know exactly how
we can escape this house.

410
00:23:35,490 --> 00:23:36,550
What kind of plan?

411
00:23:37,450 --> 00:23:39,820
I'm going to make money.
I'm going to start working.

412
00:23:40,460 --> 00:23:41,490
You?

413
00:23:42,330 --> 00:23:43,890
Don't underestimate me.

414
00:23:44,030 --> 00:23:46,430
Before I met your dad,
I took whatever work I could get...

415
00:23:46,430 --> 00:23:48,060
and worked my fingers to the bone.

416
00:23:49,170 --> 00:23:51,270
That's a fantastic idea.

417
00:23:51,430 --> 00:23:53,140
- Dad, you're home.
- Yes.

418
00:23:53,340 --> 00:23:56,410
Goodness. I worked all night
for the first time in a while,

419
00:23:56,410 --> 00:23:57,440
and my whole body aches.

420
00:23:58,070 --> 00:23:59,680
You're planning to get a job
and make money?

421
00:24:00,040 --> 00:24:01,340
I fully support that.

422
00:24:01,680 --> 00:24:03,010
In this day and age,

423
00:24:03,280 --> 00:24:05,180
you're way too young
to just stay at home.

424
00:24:05,620 --> 00:24:06,980
Let's earn money together.

425
00:24:07,250 --> 00:24:08,290
We'll save up together...

426
00:24:08,290 --> 00:24:11,450
and move to a nice, big house soon.
Okay?

427
00:24:11,990 --> 00:24:12,990
I'm hungry.

428
00:24:13,260 --> 00:24:16,190
I should eat
so I can work hard again.

429
00:24:16,960 --> 00:24:18,260
Goodness.

430
00:24:18,260 --> 00:24:21,630
I must have been a spy
in my past life.

431
00:24:22,100 --> 00:24:24,200
That's why the rest of my life
is so messed up.

432
00:24:25,170 --> 00:24:26,200
I'm heading out.

433
00:24:26,270 --> 00:24:28,310
Sweetie, you're giving up
the officetel.

434
00:24:28,370 --> 00:24:30,910
- I don't know.
- Ye Ri.

435
00:24:33,640 --> 00:24:35,480
Goodness.

436
00:24:39,250 --> 00:24:40,420
I'm downstairs, Grandma.

437
00:24:42,750 --> 00:24:44,120
Dae Chi, listen to me.

438
00:24:47,620 --> 00:24:50,460
- Yes, Grandma.
- I heard from your mother...

439
00:24:50,760 --> 00:24:53,030
that you need 200,000
to 300,000 dollars right now.

440
00:24:53,630 --> 00:24:57,130
Yes. If you could just
help me get that money,

441
00:24:57,900 --> 00:25:00,140
I can pay off the rest of my debt
within five years...

442
00:25:00,500 --> 00:25:03,410
using my salary and bonuses
while working at the company.

443
00:25:03,670 --> 00:25:05,580
I've done enough for you,

444
00:25:06,310 --> 00:25:08,650
and neither your mother
nor I have any money.

445
00:25:09,050 --> 00:25:11,580
The point is,
you need to get a second job.

446
00:25:12,220 --> 00:25:16,050
When people are in debt,
they work 2 or even 3 jobs.

447
00:25:16,920 --> 00:25:18,920
If you look around,
there's plenty of work...

448
00:25:19,060 --> 00:25:20,660
for a perfectly healthy young man.

449
00:25:21,760 --> 00:25:22,790
Pardon?

450
00:25:23,330 --> 00:25:26,760
Grandma, I'd love to do that.
But the work I do,

451
00:25:27,500 --> 00:25:29,070
by its very nature,

452
00:25:29,070 --> 00:25:31,300
makes it absolutely impossible
to take on a second job.

453
00:25:32,040 --> 00:25:33,240
You all know exactly...

454
00:25:33,970 --> 00:25:35,440
what kind of work I do.

455
00:25:36,440 --> 00:25:38,170
Yes, we know.

456
00:25:38,640 --> 00:25:39,940
You work for a big corporation.

457
00:25:40,180 --> 00:25:43,450
Yes, right. Don't you do something
with numbers at that big company?

458
00:25:43,550 --> 00:25:44,780
Something super important?

459
00:25:45,020 --> 00:25:47,780
Isn't it about picking things out
and buying them over and over,

460
00:25:47,850 --> 00:25:49,190
or something like that?

461
00:25:50,090 --> 00:25:51,090
Wait...

462
00:25:51,820 --> 00:25:55,330
Did none of you actually know
what I do for a living?

463
00:25:57,460 --> 00:25:59,530
Did you ever bother
to explain it to us?

464
00:25:59,900 --> 00:26:01,800
You just bragged
about making a lot of money.

465
00:26:02,370 --> 00:26:05,140
Yes, Da Mi is right about that.

466
00:26:05,840 --> 00:26:07,770
You just showed off
about doing important work...

467
00:26:08,310 --> 00:26:10,640
at a big company
and making tons of money.

468
00:26:11,540 --> 00:26:12,940
I won't drag this out.

469
00:26:13,480 --> 00:26:15,910
From now on, if any of you
want to eat and sleep in this house,

470
00:26:18,750 --> 00:26:20,850
you all need to pay
600 dollars a month...

471
00:26:20,920 --> 00:26:22,390
for living expenses.

472
00:26:23,490 --> 00:26:24,520
That's that.

473
00:26:24,520 --> 00:26:25,590
- Grandma!
- Grandma!

474
00:26:26,720 --> 00:26:30,060
Grandma, not me, right?
You're exempting me, aren't you?

475
00:26:30,130 --> 00:26:32,460
Da Mi, aren't you
a child of this house?

476
00:26:34,400 --> 00:26:35,400
Mother,

477
00:26:35,700 --> 00:26:38,030
asking the kids
to pay that much money...

478
00:26:38,200 --> 00:26:39,300
every single month so suddenly...

479
00:26:39,300 --> 00:26:42,740
Well, you have it easy now.

480
00:26:43,140 --> 00:26:45,980
Do I have to pay too?

481
00:26:46,310 --> 00:26:49,250
Since I manage Ri Ja's money anyway,

482
00:26:49,250 --> 00:26:51,150
you don't need to worry
about it for now.

483
00:26:52,020 --> 00:26:53,050
Dismissed.

484
00:27:02,160 --> 00:27:03,730
This is driving me crazy.

485
00:27:06,430 --> 00:27:07,460
Da Mi.

486
00:27:08,530 --> 00:27:11,600
- Da Mi.
- Mi Mi. Da Mi will be fine.

487
00:27:12,140 --> 00:27:13,670
Don't worry about her.

488
00:27:18,910 --> 00:27:20,180
I'm not fine.

489
00:27:21,010 --> 00:27:22,280
I'm really not fine.

490
00:27:26,880 --> 00:27:29,220
If I pay 600 dollars every month,
what am I supposed to live on?

491
00:27:29,620 --> 00:27:31,420
How am I supposed to study abroad?

492
00:27:32,720 --> 00:27:36,060
Grandma is being so unreasonable.
How could she do this to me?

493
00:27:42,570 --> 00:27:44,930
Da Mi, are you not
a child of this family?

494
00:27:48,540 --> 00:27:49,940
Thank you, Grandma.

495
00:27:51,170 --> 00:27:52,210
I'll be back.

496
00:28:06,320 --> 00:28:08,220
(Mission: Mompossible)

497
00:28:08,430 --> 00:28:10,790
What did you two talk about
with Da Mi yesterday?

498
00:28:10,930 --> 00:28:12,500
Something happened, right?

499
00:28:12,760 --> 00:28:16,030
How am I supposed to return this?
I need to get my tablet back too.

500
00:28:17,300 --> 00:28:18,370
What do you think?

501
00:28:18,370 --> 00:28:19,600
If I find her,

502
00:28:20,040 --> 00:28:22,870
your life will become very interesting,
don't you think?

503
00:28:24,340 --> 00:28:26,310
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
